  "description": "Erection of a New Retractable Awning Structure within the Existing Beer Garden & Redecoration Works to the Existing Pub Building. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "The tree works hereby approved shall be carried out strictly in accordance with the description on this notice of approval by a suitable qualified tree surgeon and in accordance with BS3998:2010 ‘Recommendations for tree works’ (or any standard that reproduces or replaces this standard).The maximum extents of the permitted tree work are as follows:T1: Lateral Crown Reduction: Reduce northern canopy by up to 1m to leave a canopy of 2m cutting to suitable laterals to leave a reasonable silhouette.T4: Remove epicormic growth to give 5m clear stem height.REASON:&nbsp; In the interests of visual amenity and good arboricultural practice, having regard to Policy LP51 in the Local Plan 2033 (adopted 2020).",
    "&lt;p&gt;Detailed drawings/full particulars of an external lighting scheme&amp;nbsp;must be submitted to and approved by the local planning authority, in writing,&amp;nbsp;in terms of the location of lighting and levels of luminance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect neighbouring amenities, the adjoining canal corridor, and wildlife.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "No storage of materials, mixing of concrete or other chemicals, placement of site office/welfare facilities, parking of vehicles, or plant machinery access shall take place within soft landscaped areas of the Root Protection Areas (RPAs) of any trees identified for retention, as defined in the approved document (Ref: ARB/5368/Y/200 dated Aug 2025).Specifically, the following restrictions shall apply within the RPAs for the duration of the development:No Storage: No building materials, fuels, chemicals, or equipment shall be stored or deposited.No Mixing: No mixing of mortar, cement, or use of any other deleterious substances shall occur.No Compaction: No vehicles or heavy machinery shall enter or be parked within the RPA unless on pre-approved ground protection.No Levels Change: No changes in ground levels (excavation or raising) shall be permitted without prior written consent from the Local Planning Authority.No Welfare: No site huts, toilets, or welfare units shall be placed within these areas.REASON: To accord with the requirements of Section 197(a) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 and in the interests of visual amenity, having regard to Policy LP51 in the Local Plan 2033 (adopted 2020).",
    "&lt;p&gt;The retractable roof canopy structure, hereby approved, shall thereafter be installed and maintained&amp;nbsp;in accordance with the manufacturer&#x27;s/supplier&#x27;s guidelines and recommendations as well as the External Canopy Noise Assessment (11647.RP03.PNA.1).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers and the surrounding area.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
